---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Convergence Gauge — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 76"
  description="Chullin 76: a hind leg cut above the joint is a tereifa — and so is one whose 'convergence of sinews' is removed. But which cords count? Run Abaye's four tests on six specimens, then flip switches on three strands and watch Ameimar and Mar bar Rav Ashi read the same cut two different ways."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0a0d10] !text-[#e8e3d5]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#232b32] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#141b1f]/80 to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#c9974f]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#e0b370]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 76 · 2026-07-15
      </p>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">🧵 The Convergence Gauge</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-1 text-2xl !text-[#e0b370]" dir="rtl" lang="he">וְאֵלּוּ הֵן צוֹמֶת הַגִּידִין?</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">
        A hind leg severed below the joint is kosher; above it, the animal is a <em>tereifa</em> —
        and so is one whose <strong class="!text-[#e8e3d5]">convergence of sinews</strong> is removed
        (76a:1). But a cord in flesh does not announce itself. Abaye left four tests to find it by
        feel: proud of the flesh or sunk into it, hard or soft, thick or thin, white or at least
        glassy (76a:15–16, 76b:1). Then the sages argue over how much of it has to give — one thick
        strand and two thin ones, in an ox — before the leg does too (76b:2).
        <strong class="!text-[#e8e3d5]">Today, your hands do the learning.</strong>
        Feel out six specimens, then take a knife to three strands and watch two amoraim disagree
        in real time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Instrument panel ============ -->
      <div class="mb-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#3a3320] bg-[#14120b] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9974f]">the mishnah's two doors — 76a:1–2</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370]">🖐️ Find the cord</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">Abaye's tests: prominent not sunk, hard not soft, thick not thin, white — or, per Mar bar Rav Ashi, at least glassy (76a:15–16, 76b:1).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370]">🧵 Three strands, one ox</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">One thick, two thin (76b:2). Sever enough of them and Ameimar and Mar bar Rav Ashi read the same cut two different ways.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370]">🐦 Birds get no majority</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">Sixteen strands. Sever even one, and it is a <em>tereifa</em> — no thick strand to outweigh the rest (76b:3).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370]">🦴 A break is not a cut</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">The leg can stay whole and still split Rav from Shmuel — on where it broke, and how much flesh survived (76a:2, 76b:8–9).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Game ============ -->
      <div id="game-area"></div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-[#232b32] bg-[#12171c] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9974f]">learn the real daf</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">
          Chullin 76 is butcher's law argued like philosophy: where exactly is "the leg joint" the
          mishnah means (Rav Yehuda vs. Ulla vs. Rav Pappa's reconciliation, 76a:3–9)? How far up the
          leg does the convergence of sinews run, and in what — hardness, thickness, color — does its
          identity consist? The daf never quite settles how "a majority" of three strands is counted,
          and closes with a broken bone that never fully severs, dividing Rav from Shmuel until a
          ruling is sent, reversed, and sent again from
          <a class="!text-[#e0b370] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76b.12">Eretz Yisrael</a>.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#c9974f]/40 bg-[#c9974f]/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370] hover:bg-[#c9974f]/20">Chullin 76 on Sefaria →</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin.76a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#232b32] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#8b96a0] hover:!text-[#e8e3d5]">Rashi (×74)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Chullin.76a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#232b32] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#8b96a0] hover:!text-[#e8e3d5]">Steinsaltz (×37)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Chullin.76a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#232b32] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#8b96a0] hover:!text-[#e8e3d5]">Rabbeinu Gershom (×21)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin.76a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#232b32] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#8b96a0] hover:!text-[#e8e3d5]">Tosafot (×8)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    .frank {
      font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', 'Times New Roman', serif;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .fade-in { animation: fadeIn 0.35s ease both; }
      @keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
      .gauge-needle { transition: transform 0.5s ease; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .gauge-needle { transition: none; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

    // ================= Round 1 — Identify the Cord (76a:15–16, 76b:1) =================
    const CARDS1 = [
      {
        name: 'The obvious cord',
        desc: 'It stands up proud of the flesh, feels stiff under your thumb, thick as a stylus, and gleams chalk-white.',
        answer: 'IN',
        head: 'Counts — every mark lines up',
        explain: 'Prominent, hard, thick, and white: every one of Abaye\'s tests agrees. This is the textbook convergence of sinews.',
        ref: 'Chullin 76a:16',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76a.16',
      },
      {
        name: 'Sunk from view',
        desc: 'Higher up the leg, the cords vanish — swallowed into the flesh, no longer a separate ridge you can find by feel.',
        answer: 'OUT',
        head: 'Does not count — absorbed',
        explain: 'בְּלִיעִי — once the sinews are absorbed into the flesh they are no longer reckoned, however far below they once ran.',
        ref: 'Chullin 76a:15',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76a.15',
      },
      {
        name: 'Gives like flesh',
        desc: 'It is there, and it is thick — but press it and it yields, soft as muscle.',
        answer: 'OUT',
        head: 'Does not count — soft',
        explain: 'רַכִּיכֵי — soft sinews are excluded no matter their girth. Hardness is its own, separate test.',
        ref: 'Chullin 76a:16',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76a.16',
      },
      {
        name: 'Fine as a thread',
        desc: 'Hard, prominent, chalk-white — but thin as a single strand of thread.',
        answer: 'OUT',
        head: 'Does not count — too thin',
        explain: 'קַטִּינֵי — thin sinews are out even when every other mark is right. Abaye required thickness too.',
        ref: 'Chullin 76a:16',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76a.16',
      },
      {
        name: 'Glassy, not white',
        desc: 'Thick, hard, prominent — but grey and clear, more glass than chalk.',
        answer: 'IN',
        head: 'Counts — Mar bar Rav Ashi\'s amendment',
        explain: 'Once a sinew turns translucent (זִיגִי), Mar bar Rav Ashi counts it even without true whiteness — Abaye\'s rule, widened.',
        ref: 'Chullin 76b:1',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76b.1',
      },
      {
        name: 'Dull and opaque',
        desc: 'Thick, hard, prominent — but a flat, dull grey. No shine, no white.',
        answer: 'OUT',
        head: 'Does not count — fails both tests',
        explain: 'Not white, and not glassy either: this cord fails Abaye\'s plain rule and Mar bar Rav Ashi\'s widened one alike.',
        ref: 'Chullin 76a:16',
        refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76b.1',
      },
    ];

    // ================= Round 4 — The Break (76a:2, 76b:8–9, 76b:12) =================
    function ravRuling(above, majority) {
      if (majority) return { animal: 'permitted', limb: 'permitted' };
      if (above) return { animal: 'prohibited', limb: 'prohibited' };
      return { animal: 'permitted', limb: 'prohibited' };
    }
    function shmuelRuling(majority) {
      if (majority) return { animal: 'permitted', limb: 'permitted' };
      return { animal: 'permitted', limb: 'prohibited' };
    }

    // ---- State ----
    let phase = 'r1';
    let r1idx = 0;
    let r1score = 0;
    let r1picked = null;
    let strands = { thick: false, thinA: false, thinB: false }; // false = whole, true = severed
    let r2seenThick = false;
    let r2seenThins = false;
    let r3revealed = false;
    let r4cell = null; // { above, majority }

    function dots(total, filled) {
      let out = '';
      for (let i = 0; i < total; i++) {
        out += `<span class="inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full ${i < filled ? 'bg-[#c9974f]' : 'bg-[#232b32]'}"></span>`;
      }
      return out;
    }

    function railChips() {
      const steps = [
        { key: 'r1', label: '1 · identify' },
        { key: 'r2', label: '2 · cut' },
        { key: 'r3', label: '3 · birds' },
        { key: 'r4', label: '4 · the break' },
        { key: 'end', label: 'verdict' },
      ];
      const order = ['r1', 'r1end', 'r2', 'r3', 'r4', 'end'];
      const cur = order.indexOf(phase) >= order.indexOf('r1end') ? phase : 'r1';
      const idxOf = { r1: 0, r1end: 0, r2: 1, r3: 2, r4: 3, end: 4 };
      return `<div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-1.5 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider !text-[#5a6470]">
        ${steps.map((s, i) => `<span class="rounded-full border px-2 py-0.5 ${i === idxOf[phase] ? 'border-[#c9974f]/60 !text-[#e0b370]' : 'border-[#232b32]'}">${s.label}</span>`).join('')}
      </div>`;
    }

    // ---------------- Round 1 render ----------------
    function renderR1() {
      const c = CARDS1[r1idx];
      const answered = r1picked !== null;
      let feedback = '';
      if (answered) {
        const correct = r1picked === c.answer;
        feedback = `
          <div class="fade-in mt-4 rounded-xl border p-4 ${correct ? 'border-[#7fae6c]/50 bg-[#7fae6c]/10' : 'border-[#c0453d]/50 bg-[#c0453d]/10'}">
            <p class="frank text-lg font-bold ${correct ? '!text-[#a8cf94]' : '!text-[#e8837d]'}">${correct ? '✓ Correct' : '✗ Not quite'} — ${c.head}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">${c.explain}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs !text-[#5a6470]">Source: <a href="${c.refUrl}" class="!text-[#e0b370] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]">${c.ref}</a></p>
            <button id="btn-next-card" class="mt-3 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#c9974f]/50 bg-[#c9974f]/15 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e0b370] hover:bg-[#c9974f]/25 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]">
              ${r1idx < CARDS1.length - 1 ? 'Next specimen →' : 'See your score →'}
            </button>
          </div>`;
      }
      $('game-area').innerHTML = `
        ${railChips()}
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#232b32] bg-[#12171c] p-5">
          <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
            <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9974f]">round 1 · specimen ${r1idx + 1} of ${CARDS1.length}</p>
            <div class="flex gap-1.5">${dots(CARDS1.length, r1idx)}</div>
          </div>
          <h2 class="frank text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e8e3d5]">${c.name}</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">${c.desc}</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs !text-[#5a6470]">Does it count as <span class="frank !text-[#e0b370]" dir="rtl" lang="he">צוֹמֶת הַגִּידִין</span> — the convergence of sinews?</p>
          <div id="r1-controls" class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2"></div>
          ${feedback}
        </div>`;

      if (!answered) {
        const controls = $('r1-controls');
        const inBtn = document.createElement('button');
        inBtn.className = 'rounded-xl border border-[#7fae6c]/50 bg-[#7fae6c]/10 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#a8cf94] hover:bg-[#7fae6c]/20 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]';
        inBtn.textContent = '✅ Counts';
        inBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { r1picked = 'IN'; if (r1picked === c.answer) r1score++; renderR1(); });
        const outBtn = document.createElement('button');
        outBtn.className = 'rounded-xl border border-[#c0453d]/50 bg-[#c0453d]/10 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e8837d] hover:bg-[#c0453d]/20 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]';
        outBtn.textContent = '❌ Not part of it';
        outBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { r1picked = 'OUT'; if (r1picked === c.answer) r1score++; renderR1(); });
        controls.appendChild(inBtn);
        controls.appendChild(outBtn);
      } else {
        $('btn-next-card').addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (r1idx < CARDS1.length - 1) { r1idx++; r1picked = null; renderR1(); }
          else { phase = 'r2'; render(); }
          $('game-area').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'auto', block: 'start' });
        });
        $('btn-next-card').focus();
      }
    }

    // ---------------- Round 2 render ----------------
    function gaugeSVG(kosher) {
      const angle = kosher ? -55 : 55;
      return `
        <svg viewBox="0 0 120 66" class="mx-auto block w-32" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M8 58 A 52 52 0 0 1 112 58" fill="none" stroke="#232b32" stroke-width="3" fill-opacity="0"/>
          <line class="gauge-needle" x1="60" y1="58" x2="60" y2="14" stroke="#c9974f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" style="transform-origin: 60px 58px; transform: rotate(${angle}deg);"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="58" r="4" fill="#c9974f"/>
        </svg>`;
    }

    function strandButton(key, label, heLabel) {
      const cut = strands[key];
      const cardClass = cut
        ? 'strand-btn rounded-xl border-2 px-2 py-4 text-center transition-colors border-[#c0453d]/60 bg-[#c0453d]/10 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]'
        : 'strand-btn rounded-xl border-2 px-2 py-4 text-center transition-colors border-[#c9974f]/50 bg-[#c9974f]/10 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]';
      const heClass = cut ? 'frank text-lg !text-[#e8837d]' : 'frank text-lg !text-[#e0b370]';
      const statusClass = cut ? 'mt-1 text-[10px] font-bold !text-[#e8837d]' : 'mt-1 text-[10px] font-bold !text-[#8fae6c]';
      return `<button data-strand="${key}" aria-pressed="${cut}" class="${cardClass}">
        <p class="${heClass}" dir="rtl" lang="he">${heLabel}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider !text-[#8b96a0]">${label}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-2xl">${cut ? '✂️' : '🧵'}</p>
        <p class="${statusClass}">${cut ? 'severed' : 'whole'}</p>
      </button>`;
    }

    function verdictPanel(sage, heName, kosher, reasonKosher, reasonTreifa) {
      const wrapClass = kosher
        ? 'rounded-xl border p-4 text-center border-[#7fae6c]/50 bg-[#7fae6c]/10'
        : 'rounded-xl border p-4 text-center border-[#c0453d]/50 bg-[#c0453d]/10';
      const verdictClass = kosher ? 'frank text-lg font-bold !text-[#a8cf94]' : 'frank text-lg font-bold !text-[#e8837d]';
      return `<div class="${wrapClass}">
        <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8b96a0]">${sage}</p>
        <p class="frank text-sm !text-[#c9974f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${heName}</p>
        ${gaugeSVG(kosher)}
        <p class="${verdictClass}">${kosher ? 'כְּשֵׁרָה — kosher' : 'טְרֵפָה — tereifa'}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">${kosher ? reasonKosher : reasonTreifa}</p>
      </div>`;
    }

    function renderR2() {
      const intact = ['thick', 'thinA', 'thinB'].filter((k) => !strands[k]).length;
      const majorityStructure = !strands.thick;
      const majorityCount = intact >= 2;
      const ameimarKosher = majorityStructure && majorityCount;
      const mbraKosher = majorityStructure || majorityCount;

      const onlyThickCut = strands.thick && !strands.thinA && !strands.thinB;
      const onlyThinsCut = !strands.thick && strands.thinA && strands.thinB;
      if (onlyThickCut) r2seenThick = true;
      if (onlyThinsCut) r2seenThins = true;

      let namedNote = '';
      if (onlyThickCut) {
        namedNote = `<p class="fade-in mt-3 rounded-lg border border-[#c9974f]/40 bg-[#c9974f]/10 px-3 py-2 text-xs !text-[#e0b370]">🔎 This is the Gemara's named case: sever the thick strand alone, and Ameimar and Mar bar Rav Ashi split (76b:2).</p>`;
      } else if (onlyThinsCut) {
        namedNote = `<p class="fade-in mt-3 rounded-lg border border-[#c9974f]/40 bg-[#c9974f]/10 px-3 py-2 text-xs !text-[#e0b370]">🔎 This is the Gemara's other named case: sever both thin strands, and the same two sages split the other way (76b:2).</p>`;
      }

      $('game-area').innerHTML = `
        ${railChips()}
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#232b32] bg-[#12171c] p-5">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9974f]">round 2 · cut the strands</p>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-lg !text-[#e0b370]" dir="rtl" lang="he">תְּלָתָא חוּטֵי הָווּ, חַד אַלִּימָא וּתְרֵי קַטִּינֵי</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">
            "There are three strands: one thick and two thin" — Ameimar, in the name of Rav Zevid
            (<a class="!text-[#e0b370] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76b.2">76b:2</a>).
            Tap any strand to sever it and watch both rulings update live.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-3 gap-2">
            ${strandButton('thick', 'thick', 'עָבֶה')}
            ${strandButton('thinA', 'thin A', 'דַּק')}
            ${strandButton('thinB', 'thin B', 'דַּק')}
          </div>
          ${namedNote}
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            ${verdictPanel(
              'Ameimar, name of Rav Zevid',
              'רַב זְבִיד',
              ameimarKosher,
              'Both the majority of its structure (the thick strand) and the majority of its number remain intact.',
              'Sever either the thick strand or both thin ones, and one whole majority — of structure or of number — is gone. Ameimar requires both to survive.'
            )}
            ${verdictPanel(
              'Mar bar Rav Ashi',
              'מָר בַּר רַב אָשֵׁי',
              mbraKosher,
              'Either the structural majority or the numerical majority survives — and for Mar bar Rav Ashi, one is enough.',
              'Neither majority survives this cut: the thick strand is gone and fewer than two strands remain whole.'
            )}
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#5a6470]">
            The Gemara pushes the question further still: is "a majority" the majority of just one
            strand, or a majority of each of the three (76b:4–6)? Rabbenai even transmits, in
            Shmuel's name, that a single sinew reduced to a thread no thicker than a cloak's
            drawstring is enough (76b:5–6). Same convergence, argued down to the fiber — a fight for
            another daf.
          </p>
          <button id="btn-r2-continue" class="mt-4 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#c9974f]/50 bg-[#c9974f]/15 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e0b370] hover:bg-[#c9974f]/25 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]">Continue to the birds →</button>
        </div>`;

      document.querySelectorAll('.strand-btn').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const key = btn.getAttribute('data-strand');
          strands[key] = !strands[key];
          renderR2();
        });
      });
      $('btn-r2-continue').addEventListener('click', () => {
        phase = 'r3';
        render();
        $('game-area').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'auto', block: 'start' });
      });
    }

    // ---------------- Round 3 render ----------------
    function strandChips(count, oddIndex, splitDone) {
      let out = '';
      for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        if (splitDone && i === oddIndex) {
          out += `<span class="flex h-8 w-2 rounded-full bg-[#c9974f]"></span><span class="flex h-8 w-2 rounded-full bg-[#c9974f]"></span>`;
        } else if (!splitDone && i === oddIndex) {
          out += `<button id="btn-odd-strand" class="flex h-8 w-3 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#e0b370] text-[9px] font-bold text-[#0a0d10] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#f2c14e]" aria-label="Look closer at this strand">?</button>`;
        } else {
          out += `<span class="flex h-8 w-2 rounded-full bg-[#3a3320]"></span>`;
        }
      }
      return out;
    }

    function renderR3() {
      const oddIndex = 7;
      $('game-area').innerHTML = `
        ${railChips()}
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#232b32] bg-[#12171c] p-5">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9974f]">round 3 · the bird's sixteen</p>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-lg !text-[#e0b370]" dir="rtl" lang="he">בְּעוֹפוֹת שִׁיתְּסַר חוּטֵי הָווּ</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">
            "In birds there are sixteen strands; if even one of them is severed, it is a
            <em>tereifa</em>" (<a class="!text-[#e0b370] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76b.3">76b:3</a>).
            No thick strand to outweigh two thin ones. No majority to hide behind. Mar bar Rav Ashi
            examined a bird before his father, Rav Ashi, and counted only fifteen strands —
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-4">
            ${strandChips(15, oddIndex, r3revealed)}
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-center text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#5a6470]">${r3revealed ? '16 strands, exactly as required' : 'one strand looked different — tap it'}</p>
          <div id="r3-reveal"></div>
        </div>`;

      if (!r3revealed) {
        $('btn-odd-strand').addEventListener('click', () => {
          r3revealed = true;
          renderR3();
        });
      } else {
        $('r3-reveal').innerHTML = `
          <div class="fade-in mt-4 rounded-xl border border-[#7fae6c]/50 bg-[#7fae6c]/10 p-4">
            <p class="frank text-lg font-bold !text-[#a8cf94]">✓ Two strands, fused as one</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">
              "There was one that was different from the others; he broke it apart and found it was
              two." Fifteen looked like fifteen — until the odd strand split, and the count came out
              to sixteen exactly (76b:3). In a bird, one clean cut through any single strand is all
              it takes: no majority, no thick strand to outvote the rest.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs !text-[#5a6470]">Source: <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76b.3" class="!text-[#e0b370] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]">Chullin 76b:3</a></p>
            <button id="btn-r3-continue" class="mt-3 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#c9974f]/50 bg-[#c9974f]/15 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e0b370] hover:bg-[#c9974f]/25 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]">Continue to the broken bone →</button>
          </div>`;
        $('btn-r3-continue').addEventListener('click', () => {
          phase = 'r4';
          render();
          $('game-area').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'auto', block: 'start' });
        });
      }
    }

    // ---------------- Round 4 render ----------------
    function cellButton(above, majority) {
      const active = r4cell && r4cell.above === above && r4cell.majority === majority;
      const cls = active
        ? 'rounded-xl border-2 border-[#c9974f]/70 bg-[#c9974f]/15 px-3 py-4 text-center transition-colors'
        : 'rounded-xl border-2 border-[#232b32] bg-[#0f0e09] px-3 py-4 text-center transition-colors hover:border-[#c9974f]/40';
      const label = majority ? 'majority of flesh intact' : 'majority not intact';
      const posLabel = above ? 'above the joint' : 'below the joint';
      return `<button data-above="${above}" data-majority="${majority}" class="r4-cell ${cls}">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370]">${posLabel}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider !text-[#8b96a0]">${label}</p>
      </button>`;
    }

    function renderR4() {
      $('game-area').innerHTML = `
        ${railChips()}
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#232b32] bg-[#12171c] p-5">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9974f]">round 4 · the break</p>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-lg !text-[#e0b370]" dir="rtl" lang="he">נִשְׁבַּר הָעֶצֶם, אִם רוֹב הַבָּשָׂר קַיָּים – שְׁחִיטָתוֹ מְטַהַרְתּוֹ</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">
            The mishnah's second case is not a severed leg at all — a bone can break without the leg
            coming fully apart
            (<a class="!text-[#e0b370] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76a.2">76a:2</a>).
            Rav and Shmuel split over where the break sits and how much flesh survives it. Pick a case.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
            ${cellButton(true, true)}
            ${cellButton(false, true)}
            ${cellButton(true, false)}
            ${cellButton(false, false)}
          </div>
          <div id="r4-result"></div>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-3 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#8b96a0]">
            The ruling flip-flopped: Eretz Yisrael sent word for Rav, then for Shmuel, then for Rav
            again — the break above the joint, without a majority of flesh, is a <em>tereifa</em>. The
            limb itself is not purified by the slaughter and still imparts impurity by carrying, though
            the animal is pure — merely forbidden as a <em>tereifa</em>
            (<a class="!text-[#e0b370] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.76b.12">76b:12</a>).
          </div>
          <button id="btn-r4-finish" class="mt-4 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#c9974f]/50 bg-[#c9974f]/15 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e0b370] hover:bg-[#c9974f]/25 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]">See your standing →</button>
        </div>`;

      document.querySelectorAll('.r4-cell').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          r4cell = { above: btn.getAttribute('data-above') === 'true', majority: btn.getAttribute('data-majority') === 'true' };
          renderR4();
        });
      });

      if (r4cell) {
        const rav = ravRuling(r4cell.above, r4cell.majority);
        const shmuel = shmuelRuling(r4cell.majority);
        const disagree = rav.animal !== shmuel.animal || rav.limb !== shmuel.limb;
        $('r4-result').innerHTML = `
          <div class="fade-in mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-3">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370]">Rav — 76b:8</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">Animal: <strong class="!text-[#e8e3d5]">${rav.animal}</strong> · Limb: <strong class="!text-[#e8e3d5]">${rav.limb}</strong></p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e2a1c] bg-[#0f0e09] p-3">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0b370]">Shmuel — 76b:9</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc9bb]">Animal: <strong class="!text-[#e8e3d5]">${shmuel.animal}</strong> · Limb: <strong class="!text-[#e8e3d5]">${shmuel.limb}</strong></p>
            </div>
          </div>
          ${disagree ? `<p class="fade-in mt-3 rounded-lg border border-[#c9974f]/40 bg-[#c9974f]/10 px-3 py-2 text-xs !text-[#e0b370]">🔎 This is the crux of the dispute — Rav Naḥman later challenges Shmuel on exactly this case: "A limb from which the animal lives is thrown in the garbage, and the animal itself is permitted?" (76b:10–11).</p>` : `<p class="fade-in mt-3 text-xs !text-[#5a6470]">Rav and Shmuel agree here.</p>`}
        `;
      }

      $('btn-r4-finish').addEventListener('click', () => {
        phase = 'end';
        render();
        $('game-area').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'auto', block: 'start' });
      });
    }

    // ---------------- End screen ----------------
    function renderEnd() {
      let title, note;
      if (r1score === CARDS1.length) { title = 'a butcher\'s hands'; note = 'Every specimen sorted correctly — Abaye himself would trust your thumb.'; }
      else if (r1score >= 4) { title = 'a careful feel'; note = 'Most of the tests landed. Reread the ones that didn\'t and try again.'; }
      else { title = 'still learning the cord'; note = 'The tests are precise, not intuitive — walk the specimens again.'; }

      const badges = [
        { done: true, label: `Round 1: ${r1score}/${CARDS1.length} specimens` },
        { done: r2seenThick && r2seenThins, label: r2seenThick && r2seenThins ? 'Round 2: found both named cuts' : 'Round 2: explored the strands' },
        { done: r3revealed, label: r3revealed ? 'Round 3: split the sixteenth strand' : 'Round 3: seen' },
        { done: !!r4cell, label: r4cell ? 'Round 4: judged a break' : 'Round 4: seen' },
      ];

      $('game-area').innerHTML = `
        ${railChips()}
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#232b32] bg-[#12171c] p-6 text-center">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9974f]">the gauge is put away</p>
          <p class="frank mt-2 text-3xl font-black !text-[#e8e3d5]">${r1score} / ${CARDS1.length}</p>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-xl !text-[#e0b370]">${title}</p>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-2 max-w-md text-sm !text-[#8b96a0]">${note}</p>
          <div class="mx-auto mt-4 grid max-w-sm gap-1.5 text-left">
            ${badges.map((b) => `<p class="text-xs ${b.done ? '!text-[#a8cf94]' : '!text-[#5a6470]'}">${b.done ? '✓' : '·'} ${b.label}</p>`).join('')}
          </div>
          <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
            <button id="btn-replay" class="rounded-xl border border-[#c9974f]/50 bg-[#c9974f]/15 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e0b370] hover:bg-[#c9974f]/25 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]">Run the gauge again</button>
            <button id="btn-share" class="rounded-xl border border-[#232b32] px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold !text-[#8b96a0] hover:!text-[#e8e3d5] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#c9974f]">Share score</button>
          </div>
        </div>`;

      $('btn-replay').addEventListener('click', () => {
        phase = 'r1'; r1idx = 0; r1score = 0; r1picked = null;
        strands = { thick: false, thinA: false, thinB: false };
        r2seenThick = false; r2seenThins = false; r3revealed = false; r4cell = null;
        render();
      });
      $('btn-share').addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const text = `🧵 The Convergence Gauge — Chullin 76\nIdentified ${r1score}/${CARDS1.length} specimens of tzomet ha-gidin\nhttps://matthewmiller.dev/daf/chullin-76`;
        try {
          if (navigator.share) await navigator.share({ text });
          else {
            await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
            $('btn-share').textContent = 'Copied!';
            setTimeout(() => ($('btn-share').textContent = 'Share score'), 1500);
          }
        } catch (e) { /* user dismissed share sheet */ }
      });
    }

    function render() {
      if (phase === 'r1') renderR1();
      else if (phase === 'r2') renderR2();
      else if (phase === 'r3') renderR3();
      else if (phase === 'r4') renderR4();
      else renderEnd();
    }

    render();
  </script>
</Layout>
